{
  "name": "each-time-counts-what-the-predicate-observes",
  "why": "`each_time` multiplies a penalty by the matches of the rule’s `observed` clauses (SPEC §3.2, occurrences), and both kinds that use it show what that means today. `station_required` with `each_time: true` fires for the runner who skipped the station and adds nothing: its one `observed` clause matched nothing, which is why it fired, so the runner is clean. `drafting` has no `observed` clause, so it counts one: a runner who takes 40 s through the zone twice pays two minutes once, judged on the first entry and the first exit.",
